#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:1
msgid "Tile Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:3
msgid ""
"A **tile library** (`.tilelib`) packages device functions that a kernel "
"calls like any other function: an FFT of a tile, the Cholesky factorization "
"of a tile, and so on. Tile C++ calls them through "
"`__experimental_foreign_decl__` declarations and cuTile Python through "
"`cuda.tile_preview.foreign_call`; cuTile Rust calls them through "
"`#[cutile::foreign]` declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:11
msgid ""
"Tile libraries are a public preview of Tile IR 13.5. They need a CUDA 13.5 "
"`tileiras`, and a tile library built for that same toolkit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:15
msgid "Finding tile libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:17
msgid ""
"Start with NVIDIA's [Tile IR supported-library list](https://docs.nvidia.com/"
"cuda/tile-ir/latest/sections/prog_model.html#supported-libraries). It links "
"to providers as their packages become available. Tile libraries are released "
"separately from the CUDA Toolkit; installing CUDA 13.5 alone does not "
"install every provider's `.tilelib` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:22
msgid ""
"Use the provider's installation instructions to obtain a `.tilelib` and its "
"dependencies for your toolkit. Its interface determines the function names, "
"constant arguments, shapes, types, and architectures you can use. Then "
"declare the functions as below and pass the installed paths to "
"[`TileLibrarySpec`](#configuring-tile-libraries). The provider list "
"describes Tile IR support; cuTile Rust's [current operand limitations]"
"(#limitations) also apply, including the lack of pointer operands in foreign "
"calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:30
msgid ""
"The `solver.tilelib`, `fft_path`, and provider-library paths in this chapter "
"are illustrative configuration examples. They are not bundled downloads or "
"guaranteed package filenames. Replace them with the paths and declarations "
"from the provider's package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:35
msgid "Rust SIMT functions from CUDA Oxide"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:37
msgid ""
"CUDA Oxide can also build tile libraries from Rust SIMT functions: mark them "
"with `#[tile_export]`, then package them with `cargo oxide tilelib`. See the "
"[`tilelib_relu` example](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust/blob/main/cuda-"
"oxide/crates/rustc-codegen-cuda/examples/tilelib_relu/README.md) for export "
"definitions, build commands, and current export limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:42
msgid ""
"To call these exports from cuTile Rust, write matching [`#[cutile::foreign] "
"unsafe fn` declarations](#declaring-a-foreign-function) and [configure the "
"generated `.tilelib` on the host](#configuring-tile-libraries) with "
"`TileLibrarySpec`. Match the exported function name, concrete tile shapes, "
"element types, and input/output access modes. This is device-function "
"interop: the SIMT function runs inside the Tile kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:49
msgid ""
"This uses the CUDA 13.5 preview and requires matching library, caller "
"bytecode, and `tileiras` tooling; preview libraries are not portable across "
"arbitrary toolkit versions. Oxide's current export restrictions apply in "
"addition to the [cuTile Rust limitations](#limitations). The recorded Oxide "
"execution validation used a Tile C++ caller; it does not establish an Oxide-"
"to-cuTile Rust execution test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:56
msgid "Reusable Rust kernels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:58
msgid ""
"For Rust implementations of attention, normalization, transformer utilities, "
"fused QKV, and NVFP4 MoE, see the [`cutile-kernels` catalog](https://"
"github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust/blob/main/cutile-rs/cutile-kernels/README.md) "
"and the [`nvfp4_moe` example](https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust/blob/main/"
"cutile-rs/cutile-examples/examples/nvfp4_moe.rs). The [fused QKV guide]"
"(https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-rust/blob/main/cutile-rs/cutile-examples/"
"fused_qkv.md) describes its correctness example and opt-in benchmark. These "
"are Rust source kernels launched from the host. A `.tilelib` supplies device "
"functions called from inside a kernel through `#[cutile::foreign]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:68
msgid "Declaring a foreign function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:70
msgid ""
"A foreign function is a body-less function inside a `#[cutile::module]`, "
"written like the declaration the tile library carries in its Tile IR "
"interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:74
msgid ""
"preview$func extern @cholesky<[\n"
"    Function: !cuda_tile<preview$string>, FillMode: !"
"cuda_tile<preview$string>,\n"
"    Batch: index, M: index, T: !cuda_tile<preview$Datatype>\n"
"  ]>(\n"
"    %A: tile<[Batch]x[M]x[M]xpreview$sym_t<T>> {cuda_tile.preview$access = "
"#cuda_tile<preview$access<inout>>},\n"
"    %info: tile<[Batch]xi32> {cuda_tile.preview$access = "
"#cuda_tile<preview$access<out>>}\n"
"  ) -> (tile<[Batch]x[M]x[M]xpreview$sym_t<T>>, tile<[Batch]xi32>)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:84
msgid ""
"#[cutile::module]\n"
"pub mod solver {\n"
"    use cutile::core::*;\n"
"\n"
"    /// # Safety\n"
"    ///\n"
"    /// The declaration matches `solver.tilelib`'s `cholesky`.\n"
"    #[cutile::foreign]\n"
"    pub unsafe fn cholesky<const Batch: i32, const M: i32, T: ElementType>(\n"
"        Function: &str,\n"
"        FillMode: &str,\n"
"        #[inout] A: Tile<T, { [Batch, M, M] }>,\n"
"    ) -> (Tile<T, { [Batch, M, M] }>, Tile<i32, { [Batch] }>);   // `info` "
"is output-only\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:101
msgid ""
"The declaration names a library function, not a library: the host chooses "
"the libraries a kernel links (see [Configuring tile libraries](#configuring-"
"tile-libraries))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:104
msgid ""
"`name = \"...\"` is the function's name in the library; it defaults to the "
"Rust name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:106
msgid ""
"**The constant arguments** are the `&str` parameters, then the generic "
"parameters, each group in order: a `name: &str` parameter is a string, "
"`const N: i32` an `index`, and `T: ElementType` a datatype (`f32`, "
"`f64`, ...). They correspond one to one to the constant parameters of the "
"Tile IR declaration, the template parameters of a Tile C++ declaration and "
"the `constant_params` of a cuTile Python `foreign_call`. When the library "
"orders them differently, list every name in that order with `const_args = "
"\"...\"`, e.g. `#[cutile::foreign(const_args = \"Batch, Function, M, T, "
"FillMode\")]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:115
msgid ""
"**Every other parameter is an operand the caller passes**, in the "
"declaration's order: read-only by default, read-write with `#[inout]`. "
"Scalars are rank-0 tiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:118
msgid ""
"**The results** start with the updated `#[inout]` operands. Every further "
"result is an output-only operand (`info` above): it is not a parameter, and "
"the call passes it zero-filled after the parameters. This is the form of "
"Tile C++ `__experimental_foreign_decl__` declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:122
msgid ""
"The declaration may keep the library's names (`Batch`, `A`); the lints that "
"would flag them are off for foreign declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:124
msgid ""
"A foreign function is declared `unsafe fn`, and every call is in an `unsafe` "
"block (see [Safety](#safety))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:127
msgid ""
"The declaration must match the library's interface exactly: `tileiras` "
"checks the call against the declaration the library carries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:130
msgid "Safety"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:132
msgid ""
"The compiler sees only the declaration, not the library's implementation, so "
"a foreign function is `unsafe fn`. A declaration that omits `unsafe` is an "
"error, and so is a call outside an `unsafe` block. Document the obligations "
"in a `# Safety` section of the declaration, even when there are none beyond "
"the ones below. The caller of a foreign function guarantees that:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:138
msgid ""
"The declaration matches the library's interface: the name, the constant "
"arguments and their order, the operand types and shapes, which operands are "
"`#[inout]`, and the results. `tileiras` rejects some mismatches, not all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:141
msgid ""
"The library implements the function for the target architecture and for the "
"constant arguments of the call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:143
msgid ""
"The function reads and writes only its operands and results. Foreign "
"functions take tiles, which are values, so this holds for every library "
"today. It becomes an obligation on the library once pointer operands are "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:148
msgid ""
"A wrapper that upholds these obligations for every input it accepts can be a "
"safe device function that calls the declaration in an `unsafe` block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:151
msgid "String constants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:153
msgid ""
"A string constant is a `&str` parameter. The call passes a string that the "
"JIT resolves when it compiles the kernel, as it does for the format string "
"of `print_tko`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:157
msgid "a literal: `cholesky::<1, 32, f64>(\"potrf\", \"lower\", a)`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:158
msgid ""
"a `const` item whose value is a literal, by its name or its path: `const "
"FILL: &str = \"lower\";`, `consts::FILL`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:160
msgid ""
"a local or a function parameter bound to one of these, so a wrapper can take "
"`fill: &str` and pass it on. A local reassigned inside a runtime `if`, a "
"loop, or a `{}` or `unsafe {}` block is not constant after it, or inside the "
"loop: passing it there is a compile error;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:164
msgid ""
"an associated const of a tag type, `Lower::NAME`, or `F::NAME` for a generic "
"parameter `F` bound to a tag type. When a tag type defines `NAME` in two "
"traits, name the trait: `<F as FillMode>::NAME`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:168
msgid ""
"The string becomes part of the call's specialization: two calls with "
"different strings are two different library functions. Any other expression "
"(a value computed at run time, or `concat!`) is a compile error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:172
msgid ""
"A tag type resolves by its path where it is written, as in Rust, through "
"imports and `pub use` re-exports. Two modules can each declare a `Lower` "
"whose `NAME` differs: each call passes the string of the `Lower` it names. A "
"tag that a function or method returns is the one its return type names in "
"that function's module."
msgstr ""

