#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:190
msgid "Calling a foreign function"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:192
msgid ""
"Calls look like calls to any device function, inside an `unsafe` block. "
"Generic arguments the operands determine can be inferred; the others are "
"passed with a turbofish, where `_` lets the compiler infer the rest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:196
msgid ""
"let (factor, info) = unsafe { cholesky::<_, _, _>(\"potrf\", \"lower\", "
"a_tile) };\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:200
msgid ""
"A call lowers to a Tile IR `preview$call`, e.g. `preview$call "
"@cholesky<[\"potrf\", \"lower\", 1, 32, f64]>(%a, %info0, %token)`, where "
"`%info0` is the zero-filled output-only operand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:204
msgid ""
"Foreign calls are ordered like memory accesses: a call happens after every "
"earlier load, store, atomic and call, and before every later one, including "
"across loop iterations and in inlined helpers. Accesses with no call between "
"them stay unordered, as in a kernel without foreign calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:209
msgid ""
"`#[inout]` describes how the library uses the operand: the updated value is "
"the call's result, and the caller's tile is unchanged, as with any value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:212
msgid ""
"Two modules can each declare a foreign function with the same Rust name; "
"each call reaches the one it names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:215
msgid "Configuring tile libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:217
msgid ""
"Obtain a compatible provider package through [Finding tile libraries]"
"(#finding-tile-libraries) before configuring these paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:220
msgid ""
"The host chooses the tile libraries that kernels link, so the same kernel "
"source can link a debug or a release build of a library, or one built for "
"each architecture:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:224
msgid ""
"use cutile::tile_kernel::{set_default_tile_libraries, CompileOptions, "
"TileLibrarySpec};\n"
"\n"
"// Libraries every kernel links, for the rest of the process.\n"
"set_default_tile_libraries([TileLibrarySpec::new(\"/opt/tilelibs/"
"solver.tilelib\")]);\n"
"\n"
"// A library one launch links in addition to the defaults.\n"
"let (y,) = kernels::fft_kernel(y)\n"
"    .compile_options(CompileOptions::new().tile_library(TileLibrarySpec::new(fft_path)))\n"
"    .sync()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:236
msgid ""
"The defaults (`set_default_tile_libraries`, `add_default_tile_library`) and "
"a launch's `CompileOptions::tile_library` list are combined, canonicalized, "
"sorted and de-duplicated before `tileiras` links them. A relative path is "
"relative to the current directory. Adding a library that is already a "
"default changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:241
msgid ""
"A kernel without foreign calls links nothing. A kernel with foreign calls "
"and no configured library fails to compile with an error that names the "
"library functions it calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:244
msgid ""
"An *implementation-provider* library generates code for each call with a "
"shared library it loads at link time. Declare every file it loads and every "
"setting that changes the code it generates, so the caches miss when either "
"changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:249
msgid ""
"let solver = TileLibrarySpec::new(mathdx.join(\"lib/solver.tilelib\"))\n"
"    .dependency(mathdx.join(\"lib/libmathdx_tile.so\"))\n"
"    .setting(\"mathdx-version\", \"26.01\");\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:255
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:257
msgid ""
"Operands and results are tiles and scalars; pointer operands are not "
"supported yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:259
msgid ""
"Constant parameters are `index`, string and datatype parameters; shape "
"(tuple) parameters are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:261
msgid "A tile library must have been built for the `tileiras` that links it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:262
msgid ""
"A string constant must be a literal, a `const` with a literal value, or an "
"associated const with a literal value. The JIT does not evaluate other "
"constant expressions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/tile-libraries.md:265
msgid ""
"Name resolution across modules has its own limits; see [Name Resolution](../"
"reference/dsl-api.md#name-resolution)."
msgstr ""
